# Ecosystem health (how we work)

**This file is the canonical mindset rule.** Do not duplicate it elsewhere. Per-repo `.cursor/rules/debugging.md` holds *failed experiments* and *symptom fixes* for that repo only.

**Stack and UI law:** `Repos/speculation/master-spec.md` (Read tool at task start for new sites, deploys, bootstrap, UI work).

**Solo operator:** Daryl (she/her) is the only human on this fleet. She does **not** have domain knowledge to relay technical detail. If you need an error message, log line, stack trace, deploy failure, or screenshot — **fetch it yourself**. Using her as a clipboard (paste this error, check the console, send a screenshot) is a **failed agent**, not a reasonable checkpoint.

---

## Default mode: fix and ship (MANDATORY)

**Unless Daryl explicitly opts out** in the current message (`explain only`, `don't deploy`, `plan only`, `no code`, `review only`), every request to **fix**, **address**, **heal**, **improve**, **change**, **update**, or **stop** something wrong is a **ship task**.

You are not done until production proves the fix survived.

### Ship loop (required for every ship task)

See **`agent-pipeline.mdc`** for tickets, production before/after screenshots, and branch cleanup — same pipeline for chat fixes and designer tickets.

1. **File** an `ops-agent-*` session ticket and state its ID (mandatory — even for chat-started fixes). State ticket ID in your **first response line**.
2. **Create a todo list** (mandatory) — use the TodoWrite tool with every distinct step as a task. Mark `in_progress` before starting each step, `completed` when done. Never end a turn with unmarked or pending todos for completed work. This is your accountability to other agents and to Daryl.
3. **Check for parallel agents** — before deploying to shared infrastructure (Pi, nginx, shared CSS, nginx), fetch open tickets: `GET http://localhost:3905/api/client-errors/reports?limit=20`. If another agent has an active `fixing` ticket for the same target, update your ticket summary with coordination notes. Do not deploy over in-progress work blindly.
4. **Before screenshot** on the live `https://*.dryl.io` ticket URL when one applies (`capture-agent-fix-evidence.mjs --phase before`).
5. **Fix** root cause in the **owning** repo(s) — not a partial refactor.
6. **Deploy** to production (`npm run deploy:dryl` or the repo's documented deploy command).
7. **Unblock gates** — if deploy fails on directory scripts, `@dryl/ui`, dryl-auth, or any shared gate, **fix that repo first**, then redeploy the app you touched.
8. **Verify** — deploy log + `verify-dryl-app` / `verify:console` / `verify:visual` per `directory/.cursor/rules/deploy-verify-loop.mdc`.
9. **After screenshot** on production + **Read** both before/after PNGs when a ticket is open.
10. **Resolve** ticket, merge ticket branch to `main` if used, **say done** only when the loop is clean.

### Rule precedence (breaks ties)

When instructions conflict, follow this order:

1. **This file** + `deploy-verify-loop.mdc` + user rule `dryl-production-deploy.mdc`
2. **`dryl-agent-conduct.mdc`** — never ignore failures; never offload deploy to Daryl
3. **`master-spec.md`** — UI law and anti-patterns
4. **"Minimize scope"** — only when Daryl explicitly said **no code** or **explain only**

**Questions are not review-only.** If Daryl asks "is this necessary?", "why didn't you…", or "this looks wrong", and the answer is that something is broken or badly structured: **fix it and run the ship loop**. Explanation without shipping is an unhealthy exit.

### Forbidden stops (never end a ship task here)

- "Build passed" / "lint passed" / "code looks correct"
- "Want me to deploy?" / "Should I fix directory first?" — **just do it**
- Labeling a gate failure "unrelated" or "pre-existing" without fixing the owning repo
- Offering optional follow-ups instead of finishing the loop
- Stopping after a local build when the changed app is a hosted `*.dryl.io` site
- Asking Daryl to **paste error codes**, console output, deploy logs, or screenshots you can read via tools/APIs
- Leaving open client-error groups on **https://health.dryl.io/errors** uncleared after a fix without naming why they remain
- Treating a deploy `[warn]` line as harmless — **warnings block production**. A `[warn]` in deploy output is a failed deploy. Fix the warning in the owning repo and redeploy. Do not rugsweep with "non-critical" framing. Exception: use `[info]` (not `[warn]`) for expected fallbacks that do not degrade functionality (e.g. "using built-in list"). Reserve `[warn]` for genuine degradation that must be fixed.
- Ending a ship task with todo items still marked pending — complete all todos before saying done, or explicitly cancel them with a reason.
- Describing a deploy screenshot as passing without quoting specific visible content (heading text, list items, data shown)
- Claiming an app works when the screenshot shows an empty state, error message, or loading spinner
- Treating Angular shell load as equivalent to app functionality — if the app fetches data, the data must be visible in verification
- **Adding entries to `smoke-spa-console-filters.mjs` to suppress a failing gate** — this is a gate cheat. `isIgnorableError` is for test-environment noise only (headless CORS, browser extensions, known third-party URLs). `TypeError`, `Cannot read properties of null/undefined`, or any error with a stack trace into `main-*.js` (the app bundle) can **never** be ignorable. Every entry must have a comment explaining why it is environment noise and not an app bug. Entries added to avoid fixing a crash will be reverted and the crash must be fixed.
- **Falsifying or glossing screenshot descriptions** — agents must quote specific visible text (font names, headings, list items, error messages). "Renders correctly" or "looks good" without quoting content is treated as a false pass and will be caught.
- **Layout in TS/HTML bindings** — `[style.display]`, `[style.flex]`, `[style.padding]`, `[style.width]`, `[style.height]`, `[style.margin]` and bare `style="…"` for layout belong in SCSS. Only dynamic typography (`fontFamily`, `fontWeight`, `fontSize`) may use `[style.*]` in templates.
- **Desktop-first SCSS** — `@media (max-width …)` overrides on a desktop base layout. Master spec: mobile-first base styles; desktop enhancements use `@media (min-width …)` only. `lint:mobile-first` fails deploy when violated.
- **Skipping master spec compliance gate** — reading the spec once at task start then ignoring mobile-first, file order (html → scss → ts), `@dryl/ui` components, or component decomposition because the task "looks simple" is a ship failure.

### Self-serve information (do not use Daryl as relay)

At the **start** of any fix/address/heal task, pull state yourself:

| Need | Get it yourself |
|------|-----------------|
| Errors inbox UI | **https://health.dryl.io/errors** (canonical — no local Directory inbox) |
| Open production errors | `GET https://health.dryl.io/api/client-errors?limit=50` (auth) or worker `GET http://localhost:3905/api/client-errors?limit=50` |
| Bug-report tickets | `GET https://health.dryl.io/api/client-errors/reports?limit=20` (auth) or worker `:3905` API |
| Deploy failure | `GET http://localhost:3905/api/projects/<name>/deploy-log` or `Repos/directory/logs/deploys/` |
| Gate / script output | Run the script; read stdout and exit code |
| Live page / console | `npm run verify:console`, `verify-dryl-app.mjs`, `smoke-spa-console.mjs` |
| Visual regression | Read PNG paths from `[agent-required]` block |

If `:3905` is down: `npm run start:bg` or `npm run ensure:host` from `directory` — **host fix first**, then fetch errors. Do not ask Daryl to paste what Directory would have shown.

### Shared deploy gates (always in scope)

Every `deploy:dryl` runs `smoke-spa-console`, which runs `directory/scripts/check-max-lines.mjs` on **directory scripts**. If drive-tier (or any app) deploy fails there, **split/fix directory**, then redeploy the app — same ship task, not a handoff.

