## The system must stay healthy

dryl.io is one organism: hosted apps, Directory, Pis, tunnel, error pipeline, bootstrap wiring. A single repo with green lint does **not** mean the ecosystem is healthy.

**Unhealthy exits (do not stop here):**

- Code changed but not deployed / not live-verified
- Bootstrap wiring changed but `npm run check:dryl-apps` not run
- Cross-repo health fix finished at "audit passes" without deploying affected hosted sites
- Silent failures: indistinguishable tab titles, truncated errors, missing error reporter, unwired `drylApi`
- Deploy or fleet work finished while **other apps** still have open telemetry on **health.dryl.io/errors** — without naming them and why (see **Global inbox** below)
- Deploy pipeline "succeeded" but client-error clear/verify was skipped, soft-failed, or cleared the wrong reporter `app` id
- Ship task ended on a gate failure in another repo without fixing that repo

---

## Survival instinct — definition of done

A task is done when the **live system can survive without you** in the next session.

| Scope | Agent finishes when |
|-------|---------------------|
| **Fix / address / heal request (default)** | Ship loop complete for every repo you changed |
| **Single hosted app** | `npm run deploy:dryl` + post-deploy verify + live hostname fetch (see `directory/.cursor/rules/deploy-verify-loop.mdc`) |
| **Cross-repo / fleet bootstrap** | Wiring complete + `check:dryl-apps` passes + **deploy each affected hosted site you changed** (or full fleet if Daryl asked for fleet heal) |
| **Directory / local hub** | API up on :3905, relevant scripts pass, no new client-error groups for touched apps |
| **Any deploy / fleet session** | Global inbox checked (below); touched apps clean; out-of-scope sickness **named** in the handoff |

Stopping at "build succeeded" or "lint passed" is an **unhealthy exit**.

