## Survival checks (detect → fix → prove)

Agents do not wait to be told something is sick. **Detect → fix → prove elimination** before stopping — with logs and gates, not assumptions.

### What failed last time (do not repeat)

| Blind spot | What it looked like | What actually proved health |
|------------|---------------------|-----------------------------|
| `check:dryl-apps` only | index.html has `dryl-bug-report.js` | Live `/dryl-bug-report.js` returns **200 JS**, not 302/HTML |
| `verify-bug-report-modal` on drive-tier only | drive-tier FAB OK | **Balcony `/watch`** FAB OK on its **public ingress** |
| `pi-setup-dryl-host` only | `:8080` dryl-apps.conf updated | **`balcony-443.conf :443`** updated when `balcony.origin443` (public A record bypasses tunnel) |
| No screenshots read | script exit 0 assumed | Agent **Read tool** on both PNGs + state what was verified |
| Home-page screenshot only | `verify:visual` green after `/errors` UI work | Open the **route you changed** (e.g. `https://health.dryl.io/errors`) — smoke captures `/` by default; `authPaths` is nginx-only |
| Directory API only | `:3905` reports match expectation | Production inbox is **Pi mirror** — also `GET https://<host>/api/client-errors/reports` with auth |
| Question phrasing | "is this necessary?" → explain only | Wrong structure → fix + ship loop |
| Gate in directory | "unrelated" max-lines failure | Split directory scripts, redeploy app |
| Wrong-route screenshot | "verify:console clean on `/`" | Coordinator Reads PNG for **every route that changed** (not just home) |
| Subagent fire-and-forget | "agent X completed" summary accepted | Coordinator personally Reads live PNG + reference before ticket resolve |
| Lint-pass-as-done | "lint/build passed, done" | UI ship = visual match on live changed route, not gate exit codes |
| Screenshot read vague | Agent said "renders correctly" after reading deploy PNG | Agent **quotes specific visible text** from PNG — list items, headings, data — and explicitly states no error/empty states visible |
| Data-driven app shell load | `verify-dryl-app` exit 0, smoke exit 0 | For apps that fetch external data on load: screenshot or browser confirms **data is present** (not spinner, not "failed to load", not "0 results") |
| Silent data fetch failure | App shows "Failed to load" UI, Directory inbox empty, all pipeline gates green | `catchError` in data services calls `drylReportError` — error visible in health.dryl.io/errors inbox |

`check:dryl-apps` = wiring audit. **Not** live survival.

### Visual verification (UI work)

After any UI change, the coordinator (not a subagent) must:

1. **Open the specific changed route** in browser — not just `/`. Use browser MCP or `verify:console` with the exact path.
2. **Take a screenshot**, **Read the PNG**, and compare to any reference image Daryl provided. State what you saw.
3. **Subagent completion ≠ visual proof.** A Task subagent's "completed" message is not evidence. The coordinator must Read the live PNG for every changed route before resolving a ticket.
4. **Lint/build/console-exit-0 are wiring gates, not design acceptance.** UI work is not done until the changed route visually matches intent on production.
5. **"Global overrides" / "override tokens globally"** always means `:root` in a global stylesheet — never page-scoped. After a `:root` token change, verify ALL app routes that consume those tokens, not just the one you edited.
6. **User is never visual QA.** Use browser MCP to open the live URL, screenshot, Read, compare, fix, redeploy. Daryl sending screenshots = failed agent.

**Forbidden:** resolving an ops-agent ticket or saying "done" while known visual breakages remain, even if all automated gates pass.

### Mandatory gate (shared addons / bug hunter / nginx)

After `deploy:shared`, `pi-setup-dryl-host`, or any bug-hunter/nginx touch:

```bash
cd directory && npm run verify:bug-hunter-canary
```

This script:

1. **Probes** every entry in `dryl-static-sites.json` → `bugHunterCanaries` (currently: `drive-tier`, `balcony` `/` + `/watch` when `origin443`, `cycles`, `candles`) — `/dryl-bug-report.js` and `/api/dryl/auth/me` must not redirect or return HTML.
2. **Opens FAB** on each canary URL (auth screenshot flow) and saves PNGs.
3. **Exits non-zero** on any failure — deploy is not done.

Fast probe only (no FAB): `npm run heal:fleet:probe` or `node directory/scripts/verify-bug-hunter-canary.mjs --probe-only`

**Add canaries in the manifest** — do not hardcode new hosts in scripts. Use `whenOrigin443: true` for balcony-only paths.

**Agent finish line for bug-hunter work:** canary gate green + **Read both** `directory/logs/deploy-screenshots/bug-reporter/latest-modal-*.png` + name what you saw. Do not claim healed without this.

### Multi-ingress rule

One hostname can have **more than one live nginx path**. If `balcony.origin443` is true, public traffic uses `balcony-443.conf` on `:443`, not `dryl-apps.conf` on `:8080`. `pi-setup-dryl-host.py` now chains `pi-setup-balcony-443.py --nginx-only` when that flag is set; still run the canary gate to prove it.

